Wine: provide AMD driver queries only to the verified AoE IV launch

Backport Proton's ADL implementation, unchanged, from ValveSoftware/wine
0be231deb686bc9c9dd15dae836baa5b3b02150e (LGPL-2.1-or-later):
https://github.com/ValveSoftware/wine/tree/0be231deb686bc9c9dd15dae836baa5b3b02150e/dlls/atiadlxx
The package moves atiadlxx.dll out of Wine's global builtin directories into
engine/share/wine/aoe4/driver-compat/<arch>-windows/. After 0032's descriptor
hash/layout verification succeeds, only that AoE IV process adds the private
folder to its builtin search path and resolves the private PE module through
a gated Unix loader call (no prefix placeholder is installed). No environment variable or registry path
is written; children and other games do not inherit the directory. HB_AOE4=1
is required and HB_AOE4_ADL=0 turns this part off. A missing module leaves the
normal driver check in place. No game file is replaced.

AoE IV's native AGS 6.2 reports AGS_NO_AMD_DRIVER_INSTALLED without ADL.
With this implementation it returns compatibility driver metadata. The local
DLL trial reached the main menu, kept the Gen7 Only performance class and
changed no graphics setting. This does not claim AMD hardware or extensions.

